# Numee Monorepo

## Workspace layout

- `apps/candidate` — candidate Next.js app (port **3000**)
- `apps/api` — NestJS API + Prisma (port **3001**)
- `apps/admin` — Vite React admin (port **3002**)
- `apps/recruiter` — recruiter Next.js app (port **3003**)
- `packages/shared` — `@numee/shared` UI, types, and pure utils

## Conventions

- Package names use `@numee/*` (`@numee/candidate`, `@numee/api`, `@numee/admin`, `@numee/recruiter`, `@numee/shared`)
- Package manager: **pnpm**; task runner: **turbo**
- Prisma lives **only** in `apps/api` — never in frontends or shared
- No secrets in `packages/shared` or frontend apps; keep secrets in `apps/api` / root env consumed by the API
- Dev ports: candidate `3000`, API `3001`, admin `3002`, recruiter `3003`

## Portal sessions

- Use **separate cookie names per portal** (`numee_candidate_session`, `numee_recruiter_session`, `numee_admin_session`). Never share a single `session` cookie across portals.
- Keep `/api` **same-origin proxies** (Next rewrites / Vite proxy) so cookies stay on each app’s origin in local and typical deployments.
- Each portal has its **own login UI and login endpoint**. Do not sign admins or recruiters in via candidate auth (`POST /api/auth/login` rejects those roles).
- Nest `SessionGuard` resolves the cookie from the request path (`/api/admin/*`, `/api/recruiter/*`, else candidate).
- Cookie name constants live in `@numee/shared` (`PORTAL_SESSION_COOKIES`); API setters and frontend readers must stay aligned.

## Commenting / JSDoc

Document exported and public APIs with short `/** … */` blocks (1–3 sentences) focused on why, invariants, and side effects. Prefer TypeScript types over `@param` / `@returns` noise.

**Document:** package exports (`@numee/shared` types, constants, utils, components); Nest route handlers (intent / auth / side effects); Nest services and processors (public methods + non-obvious builders); frontend `lib/` helpers and non-obvious component props/behavior — especially portal auth helpers, guards, login gates, and session cookie utilities.

**Skip:** private one-liner helpers and trivial mappers; thin page shells / presentational wrappers where names + types suffice; generated/config (`next-env.d.ts`, Vite env, Prisma client, prompt blobs).

Do not add ESLint `require-jsdoc` or Typedoc/Swagger gates for this convention.
